# SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
# Omarchy Mobile storage guard, continued in Arch. The initramfs marks every UFS
# partition read-only except userdata (dipper is not A/B: there is one `boot`,
# one `system` and one `userdata`, so nothing else is ever written). udev would
# recreate the whole-disk nodes, so make them inaccessible and keep desktop
# tools away from every Android partition.
#
# dipper spreads its partitions over six LUNs, sda to sdf, with userdata on sda.
SUBSYSTEM=="block", KERNEL=="sd[a-f]", MODE="0000", ENV{UDISKS_IGNORE}="1"
SUBSYSTEM=="block", KERNEL=="sd[a-f][0-9]*", ENV{ID_PART_ENTRY_NAME}!="userdata", ENV{UDISKS_IGNORE}="1"
